Looking at the cuboid (2×2×5), the white cubes visible on the top back row must connect down into the hidden bottom‑back row. The only way to complete a connected 5‑cube white piece (while keeping the black, light grey and dark grey pieces connected with five cubes each) is for the white piece to occupy a 2×2 square block (the two visible white top cubes plus the two cubes directly beneath them) plus one extra cube attached in the same plane at the end of the block.

This is exactly the shape shown in diagram E: a 2×2 square of cubes with one cube attached in‑plane at a corner (after a 180° rotation in the plane of the square).

